# Gestures and page scrolling

Configure image gestures on the cropper and stencil gestures on its child. They are separate interaction surfaces.

## Choose input methods

| Prop | Options |
| --- | --- |
| `moveImage` | Boolean, or `mouse` and `touch` flags. |
| `scaleImage` | Boolean, or `touch` and `wheel`; wheel may contain a `ratio`. |
| `rotateImage` | Boolean, or a `touch` flag. Touch rotation defaults to off. |

Image movement and scaling are enabled by default. For example, keep touch zoom but allow the mouse wheel to scroll the page:

```svelte
<Cropper {src} scaleImage={{ touch: true, wheel: false }} />
```

Use `movable`, `resizable`, `handlers` and `lines` on the [stencil](/docs/guides/stencils). Cropper `disabled` blocks user interactions throughout the cropper; programmatic methods remain available.

## Let the page scroll

Replace the `backgroundWrapper` snippet when the rule depends on the event. The example leaves a plain wheel or one-finger swipe to the page, then accepts Ctrl + wheel or two fingers for image manipulation.

<Example source={CropperScrollExampleSource} title="CropperScrollExample" files={{ 'BackgroundWrapperWithNotifications.svelte': CropperScrollExampleFile0 }}>
	<CropperScrollExample />
</Example>

<CodeBlock html={wrapperSource.html} code={wrapperSource.code} />

The wrapper composes `CropperBackgroundWrapper` and uses its `onEvent` callback. Calling `preventDefault()` on the supplied `TransformableImageEvent` vetoes the image transform. This differs from calling it on the native event, which prevents the browser's own action. Accepted image gestures should not also scroll the page.

## Finish interactions

The cropper reports `onInteractionStart` and `onInteractionEnd`, as well as move, resize and image-transform callbacks. Custom controls must call the matching end method when their gesture finishes so reconciliation and interaction UI can settle.

The gesture primitives use native non-passive listeners installed through `{@attach}`. When forwarding movement callbacks, preserve the native event: resizing uses it for modifier keys. Use [HandlerWrapper and LineWrapper](/docs/reference/stencil-primitives) when replacing stencil controls so their event behaviour remains intact.
